  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing MPCA for winterization to families in NWS (DEC Ph2+ACT top up 57kUSD)  - Molham Team</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome B &#x2013; Families affected by the earthquake and IDPs receive 150 USD one off MPCA cash assistance &#xa0;

Through this MPCA intervention, Molham aims not only to address target groups immediate needs but to also restore some sense of dignity and security.&#xa0; This cash assistance will empower families to make decisions based on their most pressing needs, whether it&apos;s purchasing food, or obtaining essential services.&#xa0;&#xa0;


Output B1.2.1 &#x2013; People and communities affected by crisis are provided with one-off $150 USD Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) &#x2013; Aleppo (target 190 HH/ families)&#xa0;


&#xa0;


Providing the IDP families and vulnerable communities affected by earthquake who are leaving in harsh conditions and most in need in Idleb with MPCA to prioritize and met a set of needs unique to their households after moving to designated Molham Residential Villages/ Apartments.&#xa0;&#xa0;


&#xa0;


Output B2.3.2 &#x2013; People and communities affected by crisis are provided with one-off $150 USD Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA)&#xa0;&#x2013; Idleb (target 500 families)&#xa0;&#xa0;


Providing the IDP families and vulnerable communities affected by earthquake who are leaving in harsh conditions and most in need in Aleppo with MPCA to prioritize and met a set of needs unique to their households after moving to designated Molham Residential Villages/ Apartments.</narrative>
  </description>
